<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Republican People's Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded <a href="/years/1923">1923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CHP, Cumhuriyet Halk Partisi, People's Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Republican People's Party (CHP) is the oldest political party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</a>. It grew out of the resistance groups of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkish-war-of-independence">Turkish War of Independence</a>, united at the 1919 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a> Congress, and was founded as the People's Party in 1923. In the one-party period it carried out sweeping reforms, among them strict secularism, women's suffrage and the switch of written Turkish to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> script, while suppressing opposition and Kurdish resistance to assimilation. Its logo, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-six-arrows">Six Arrows</a>, stands for the principles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kemalism">Kemalism</a>. After losing the 1950 election it handed over power peacefully; banned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/military-junta">military junta</a> of 1980, it was re-established in 1992.</p></div>
